# Boxes that scroll: the wheel over a pane moves the pane and not the page,
# a pane with nothing left passes the notch on, the keyboard follows
# whatever the reader last moved, a scrollbar thumb can be dragged, and a
# box that only clips gives a reader no way in.
#
# The content area starts 76 px down (tab strip + toolbar) and 0 px in. The
# page below puts a 302x102 pane at the body's 8 px margin, so window
# (200, 160) is page (200, 84) and inside it; the clip box below it spans
# page y 110 to 172. No colour may be written as #rgb here: a # in a data
# URL starts its fragment and the rest of the page is lost.
resize 800 500
open data:text/html,<title>Panes</title><style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}.pane{width:300px;height:100px;overflow:auto;border:1px solid gray}.clip{width:300px;height:60px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid gray}.tall{height:400px;background:lavender}.spacer{height:900px}</style><div class="pane"><div class="tall">pane one</div></div><div class="clip"><div class="tall">clipped</div></div><div class="spacer">below</div>
assert-title Panes
assert-scroll 0
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 0

# A notch over the pane moves the pane, and leaves the page where it was.
wheel-at 200 160 -1
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 60
assert-scroll 0
assert-golden goldens/scroll-pane.png

# The keyboard follows the pane the wheel last moved.
key Down
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 120
assert-scroll 0

# End takes the pane to its far edge and no further: 400 tall inside a
# 100 px scrollport leaves 300 to reach.
key End
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 300
assert-scroll 0

# With nothing left, a further notch over the pane passes to the page. The
# page moves 60 under the window, so the pane is now read at window 116.
wheel-at 200 160 -1
assert-box-scroll 200 116 0 300
assert-scrolled

# A box that only clips gives a reader no way in, so a notch over it is the
# page's own. The clip box spans page y 110 to 172, which is window 186
# to 248 while the page stands at zero.
key Home
wheel-at 200 200 -1
assert-box-scroll 200 200 0 0
assert-scrolled

# The pane's own bar: 12 px wide down the scrollport's right edge, which
# ends at page x 309, so 303 is on it. The pane shows a quarter of its
# content, so the thumb is a quarter of the 100 px track — page y 9 to 34,
# window 85 to 110. Taking hold of it and dragging past the track's foot
# puts the pane at its far edge.
key Home
wheel-at 200 160 5
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 0
drag 303 95 303 400
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 300
assert-golden goldens/scroll-thumb.png

# A click on the track below the thumb moves a scrollport at a time,
# towards the pointer.
key Home
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 0
click 303 126
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 100

# A pane that can only move across takes a plain wheel that way — the wide
# table in a narrow column, which is what the whole of this is for. The
# pane is 302x42 at the body's margin, so window (200, 101) is page
# (200, 25) and inside it; 900 px of content inside a 300 px scrollport
# leaves 600 to reach.
open data:text/html,<title>Across</title><style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}.across{width:300px;height:40px;overflow:auto;border:1px solid gray}.long{width:900px;height:20px;background:lavender}</style><div class="across"><div class="long">a long strip</div></div>
assert-title Across
assert-box-scroll 200 101 0 0
wheel-at 200 101 -1
assert-box-scroll 200 101 60 0
assert-scroll 0
# Ten more notches would be 660; the pane stops at the 600 it has.
wheel-at 200 101 -10
assert-box-scroll 200 101 600 0
assert-golden goldens/scroll-across.png

# Find in page reaches into a box that scrolls: the word sits 300 px down a
# 100 px pane, so moving the page alone could never bring it into sight.
# The pane is 302x102 at the body's margin — window (200, 160) is page
# (200, 84), inside it — and it has 288 to reach.
open data:text/html,<title>Reach</title><style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}.pane{width:300px;height:100px;overflow:auto;border:1px solid gray}.gap{height:300px}</style><div class="pane"><p>top of the pane</p><div class="gap"></div><p id="deep">buried</p></div><div style="height:900px">below</div>
assert-title Reach
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 0
key ctrl+f
type buried
assert-find 1 of 1
key Escape
# The pane moved until the word met its bottom edge; the page had no need
# to move at all, which is the point.
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 287
assert-scroll 0

# A fragment link into the same pane moves it too, and the page after it —
# the target's own box, so it reaches the pane's far edge. With the page at
# 89 the pane is read at window 90.
wheel-at 200 160 20
assert-box-scroll 200 160 0 0
navigate data:text/html,<title>Reach</title><style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}.pane{width:300px;height:100px;overflow:auto;border:1px solid gray}.gap{height:300px}</style><div class="pane"><p>top of the pane</p><div class="gap"></div><p id="deep">buried</p></div><div style="height:900px">below</div>#deep
assert-scroll 89
assert-box-scroll 200 90 0 288
